  "witness": "Take r=1, F(x)=2x ∈ ℤ[x], and p=2. F is nonconstant and deg(F)=1. For both residues x∈𝔽₂={0,1}, F(x)=2x≡0 (mod 2), so c₂(F)=2. The claimed bound is deg(F)·2^(1−1)=1. Thus 2≤1 is false."
